<body>
<header>
  <h1>DevOps, CI/CD & Infrastructure as Code</h1>
  <p class="meta">Author: Rosario Roussin · Last updated: 2025-09-28</p>
</header>
<section class="toc">
  <h2>On this page</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="#pipeline">A simple CI/CD pipeline that works</a></li>    <li><a href="#iac-choice">Terraform or CloudFormation?</a></li>    <li><a href="#minimal-iam">Minimal IAM for deploy‑only automation</a></li>  </ul>
</section>
<section id="pipeline">
  <h2>A simple CI/CD pipeline that works</h2>
  <p class="answer">Use repo PRs with checks, build and test on each commit, and deploy to dev automatically. Promote to prod with approvals and change logs. Store secrets in a managed vault and rotate regularly to reduce risk.</p>
  <h3>Steps</h3>
  <ol>
    <li>Require PR reviews; run tests on push.</li>
    <li>Build artifact/image; scan for vulnerabilities.</li>
    <li>Auto‑deploy to dev; gated release to prod.</li>
    <li>Store secrets in a managed service; rotate.</li>
  </ol>
</section>
<section id="iac-choice">
  <h2>Terraform or CloudFormation?</h2>
  <p class="answer">Terraform offers multi‑cloud and a large module ecosystem; CloudFormation is AWS‑native and integrates tightly with IAM and service features. Pick one and standardize to prevent drift and duplication. Modules/stacks keep configurations re‑usable and consistent.</p>
  <h3>Steps</h3>
  <ol>
    <li>Pick a standard and stick to it.</li>
    <li>Create reusable modules/stacks.</li>
    <li>Validate plans/changes in CI before apply.</li>
    <li>Run drift detection on a schedule.</li>
  </ol>
</section>
<section id="minimal-iam">
  <h2>Minimal IAM for deploy‑only automation</h2>
  <p class="answer">Grant automation only what it needs: deploy to specific services, read secrets, read logs. Avoid wildcard admin. Scope by resource ARNs, use conditions where possible, and log all actions for traceability.</p>
  <h3>Steps</h3>
  <ol>
    <li>List exact actions required by the pipeline.</li>
    <li>Scope permissions to resource ARNs.</li>
    <li>Attach role to CI runner; short session duration.</li>
    <li>Log and review changes regularly.</li>
  </ol>
  <h3>Snippet</h3>
  <pre><code>{
  "Version":"2012-10-17",
  "Statement":[{
    "Effect":"Allow",
    "Action":["ecs:UpdateService","iam:PassRole","ecr:*","logs:CreateLogStream","logs:PutLogEvents"],
    "Resource":"*"
  }]
}</code></pre>
</section>
</body>
